<title>GERMANY: ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S DOWNHILL TRAINING CALLED OFF.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S DOWNHILL TRAINING CALLED OFF.</headline>
<dateline>GARMISCH-PARTENKIRCHEN, Germany 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wednesday's first training run for a men's World cup skiing downhill on Saturday was cancelled due to fresh snow, organisers said.</p>
<p>A heavy snowfall overnight left organisers unable to clear loose snow from the Kandahar piste in time. They were optimistic, however, that it would be possible to hold a training run on Thursday.</p>
</text>
